  "id": "COMPOUND:24562 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanistic link between 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone and Carboxylesterase 2, mediated through Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and other targets. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which indicate that 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone acts as a target for various compounds that ultimately inhibit Carboxylesterase 2. The shared target of these compounds—Thioredoxin, mitochondrial—suggests a common biological pathway, possibly involving oxidative stress or mitochondrial function. The presence of multiple independent targets, including Diplotrin A, 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, and Flavipin, further supports the idea that 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may influence cellular processes that are relevant to Carboxylesterase 2 activity. The integration of these pathways implies that 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone could modulate cellular processes that are critical for Carboxylesterase 2 function, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
